    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0753" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/970a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-15T19:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1934—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. On May 16 Japanese Ambassador handed me a “secret and confidential”
                        memorandum<anchor n="40" xml:id="d557-f1"/> purporting to represent certain
                    “private thoughts” suggesting that the American and Japanese Governments make a
                    “joint declaration” of policy. On May 29 I informed him orally but definitely
                    that we could not adopt that suggestion. Details follow by pouch.</p>
                <p>On June 13 the Ambassador was received by the President in farewell call. I was
                    present. No matters of policy discussed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
